        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF150 supports <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/caretRangeFromPoint\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\"> Document.caretRangeFromPoint()</code></a>. This is non-standard, so primarily for parity reasons.<br>\nDevelopers should prefer <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/caretPositionFromPoint\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">caretPositionFromPoint()</code></a> when supported \"generally\" because it is shadow root aware (but not on FF, which doesn't support the option according to BCD).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note, and also updates the docs to explain why you should prefer <code class=\"notranslate\">caretPositionFromPoint()</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4127666989\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43550\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43550/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43550\">#43550</a></p>",
